    fix: ValueError in get_all_records when ChromaDB returns numpy embedding array
    
    ChromaDB returns embeddings as a numpy ndarray, not a Python list.
    The previous code used:
        embeddings = res.get("embeddings") or []
    NumPy raises:
        ValueError: The truth value of an array with more than one element
        is ambiguous. Use a.any() or a.all()
    because `or` evaluates truthiness of the full array.
    
    Fix: check `is not None` explicitly instead of relying on truthiness,
    and wrap the per-row list() conversion in try/except to handle any
    remaining edge cases from ChromaDB version differences.
    
    This was crashing both the EvictionThread and the /api/mind/snapshot
    route, causing a 500 on every visualization load.
    
