    fix: 3D mind scene blank due to zero-height grid container at mount time
    
    Two root causes:
    1. .app-grid had no grid-template-rows or explicit height, so .panel-mind
       collapsed to 0px — root.clientHeight returned 0 when scene.ts ran and
       the WebGL backbuffer was created at 0×500 (placeholder) then never
       properly resized before first render.
    
    2. renderer.setSize() was called once at mount with clientWidth/Height that
       could both be 0 because DOM layout hadn't completed yet.
    
    Fixes:
    - styles.css: add grid-template-rows:1fr + height:100% + min-height:0 to
      .app-grid so the centre column fills the available height; add
      height:100% + min-height:0 to .panel-mind.
    - scene.ts: initialise renderer at 1×1 (no-op placeholder), extract
      onResize() helper used by both ResizeObserver and a single
      requestAnimationFrame call right after mount so the backbuffer is
      correctly sized on the next frame after layout completes.
    
